start() can throw (NotSupportedError / InvalidStateError on some Android WebViews and Samsung Internet where isTypeSupported returns true but start rejects the codec). The throw escapes an async function called from an onclick, so it becomes an unhandled rejection: state stays 'listening', the live card stays up, the timer and the waveform keep running (the meter is fed by the AudioContext, not the recorder), and nothing is being captured.

