Use rewrites, NOT "cleanUrls": true. Vercel's routing order runs the filesystem check before rewrites, so /game.html keeps serving directly (200, no redirect) and only the unmatched /game falls through to the rewrite. That means: no redirect hop on in-app nav, og:url on game.html:12 stays canonical and correct, and sw.js:11's precache of '/game.html' still matches the URL users actually navigate to. cleanUrls would invert all three — it 308s /game.html to /game, so the precached '/game.html' entry becomes unreachable and an offline visit to the game falls through to caches.match('/') at sw.js:59 and renders the accent page instead.

Do not change any href in index.html, game.html, privacy.html, sw.js, or manifest.webmanifest. /game.html remains the canonical URL; /game becomes an additional working alias.

