Make the replacement obey the same place rule `dealDeck` obeys, and mirror `dealDeck`'s own documented fallback ("if a deck is too thin to avoid it, it falls back to filling the round rather than dealing short") so a thin deck still gets a playable clip instead of the one that just failed.

Before:
```js
function replacementClip() {
  const used = new Set(deck.map((c) => c.id));
  const pool = (window.CLIPS[gameType] || []).filter((c) => !used.has(c.id));
