`min-width: 0` only lets the flex item shrink; it does nothing to the grid track inside it. The implicit column is auto-sized, and an auto track's minimum resolves to min-content (56.7px, floored by .listens), so the children overflow the collapsed 19px box. `minmax(0, 1fr)` sets the track minimum to 0 so the children track the container box instead. Verified by full-face elementFromPoint scan: scrub-stolen area goes 390px² -> 0px² at 280px, 320px, and 360px viewports.

